# A script that starts a hidden task while it loads (`mnml.task.run` in
# its init.lua — a build watcher, a linter) must not keep mnml from
# quitting. The task used to start inside `App.initWith`, on the App
# that function then returned by value: the worker reported to a task
# group nobody owned any more, and the moved App's shutdown waited for
# it forever — Ctrl+Q, SIGTERM and the end of this file all hung.
#
# The script is a dev-root fixture named by the environment, so it is
# there before the App is built (a file written by a step is too late).
# The task still runs, in the workspace; the file then ends, and the
# runner's teardown is the quit under test: a hang is this file's
# timeout.
# env: MNML_SCRIPTS_DEV_ROOTS=${MNML_REPO}/tests/e2e/fixtures/init_task
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
wait 300
expect file INIT_TASK_RAN contains "ran"
